                                                "sense_id": "2827a78a-caec-3f4c-a85f-734b47cac2bd",
                                                "text": "No matter how melodramatic the story behind the music might be, most audiences won't buy atonalism; Arnold Schoenberg could have been devoured by escaped circus tigers while he was finishing the Variations for Orchestra and it would still get booed off the stage."
                                            },
